Use case: stylized-concept. Produce a production sprite ATLAS for a 2D oblique Chinese historical strategy map. Reference image 1 is the approved Tongguan v5 art direction. Reference image 2 is the original pen-and-flat-color drawing reference. Match their casual expressive pen strokes with correct underlying structure, selective detail and very PALE muted colors. No polished rendering, no 3D shading, no ornate parchment, no micro-detail. The atlas itself must have a genuinely TRANSPARENT alpha background, not white, cream, grey or painted checkerboard. No labels, letters, numbers, border, grid lines, watermark, cast shadow, ground rectangle or full landscape. Each sprite is isolated from every other sprite with at least 10% empty margin inside its own cell. Do not let any stroke cross a cell boundary. Use a consistent fixed oblique map view. Draw complete silhouettes and don't crop any object.
Asset: ONE foliage atlas, landscape aspect ratio 3:2, ideally 1536x1024. Exactly 3 equal columns by 2 equal rows, SIX complete isolated tree-group sprites, each centered in its own cell.
Read order left-to-right then top-to-bottom:
1 broad, lopsided spreading deciduous tree with small crown gaps and an exposed crooked forked trunk;
2 a loose cluster of three slender upright trees of different heights, crowns distinctly narrow and asymmetric;
3 two riverside willow-like trees with sweeping hanging branches and irregular broken crown outlines;
4 a group of two pine trees with open, loosely tiered flat crowns and visibly different branches;
5 a dense irregular grove of mixed broadleaf trees, with overlapping crowns, one taller sparse tree and a ragged edge;
6 low wide shrubs with one small gnarled open-branched tree, sparse and low.
Every cell must have a genuinely different silhouette and branch structure. Irregular crown lines, a few interior pen marks, simple flat pale grey-olive/sage green washes. Trunks muted brown-grey. No black masses of individually drawn leaves. No green saturation. There should be transparent gaps between branches. No broad patch of ground beneath the trees. These will be stamped onto an existing map, not used as rectangular illustrations.

