Asset: ONE landform atlas, landscape aspect ratio 3:2, ideally 1536x1024. Exactly 3 equal columns by 2 equal rows, SIX complete isolated landform sprites, each centered in its own cell.
Read order left-to-right then top-to-bottom:
1 a broad rounded mountain shoulder with an off-center ridge, a secondary low spur and an open foothill;
2 an elongated gently winding ridge with a low saddle and different-height shoulders;
3 an irregular steep crag with two unequal rock summits, exposed pale cliff face and low sloping base;
4 a long rocky escarpment with an uneven cliff edge and rounded hill above it;
5 a pair of gentle broad low hills with different slopes and a shallow saddle, much lower than the upper-row mountains;
6 a spreading low foothill with a few rock outcrops, curved flank and open gently tapering ends.
Use sparse broken structural pen strokes following the slopes, not a dense engraving texture. Fills VERY LIGHT: pale warm stone beige and extremely pale grey-sage, as in v5. Colors must be light and diluted, not dark desaturated slate. More variation in silhouettes than in texture. Transparent outside each mountain shape, no rectangular ground or paper background. Avoid rows of pointed identical triangles, dramatic shadows, or thick black bottom outlines. Do not add trees, buildings, paths or labels. Natural irregular contours on accurately drawn volumes.
